 % [before 2026-11-17: only the pending-squash leak] \noindent\textbf{A known bug we miss.} \toolname{} misses the pending-squash timing leak that Protean's authors found in the branch-resolution logic STT and SPT share~\cite[\S VII-B4b]{protean}. STT's repository fixed it in commit 18e304f~\cite{nickscommittoSTT}, but our SPT build, AMuLeT's STT build, and our STT build at commit e3283b9~\cite{sttrepo} predate the fix, and we run tests on all three. When an older tainted branch and a younger untainted branch mispredict in the same cycle, the issue stage reports only the older one, whose squash the defense holds until the branch is safe, so whether the younger branch squashes at once leaks the tainted branch's outcome. It needs two mispredicted branches to resolve in the same cycle, and the harness's resolution holds rarely end in the same cycle.
 \noindent\textbf{Known bugs we miss.} \toolname{} misses two bugs that Protean's authors found. The first is a pending-squash timing leak in the branch-resolution logic STT and SPT share~\cite[\S VII-B4b]{protean}. STT's and SPT's repositories fixed it~\cite{nickscommittoSTT,mosier2025sptpr4}, but our SPT build, AMuLeT's STT build, and our STT build at commit e3283b9~\cite{sttrepo} predate the fix, and we run tests on all three. When an older tainted branch and a younger untainted branch mispredict in the same cycle, the issue stage reports only the older one, whose squash the defense holds until the branch is safe, so whether the younger branch squashes at once leaks the tainted branch's outcome. It needs two mispredicted branches to resolve in the same cycle, and the harness's resolution holds rarely end in the same cycle. The second is an untaint bug in SPT~\cite[\S VII-B4c]{protean}: after a fault reaches commit, the core can still execute transient loads that never enter the ROB, so their outputs stay untainted, and SPT's shadow-L1 logic untaints the L1D bytes they access, which may hold secrets. Our SPT build predates its fix~\cite{mosier2025sptpr6}, but the bug needs a fault pending at commit, which our tests are not built to produce.
